From ff0f33d9364bda91d946917350ec07f73ad06c71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:22:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): cut a level at the tab top so a contour tab is
 tab_height tall

A closed-ring 2D Contour carries its tabs on each level below
bottom_z + tab_height. The last level above that plane cut the whole
ring, so a tab stood up to that level: 4 mm with a 4 mm stepdown and a
1.5 mm tab height.

ContourParams::ring_levels adds the tab top as a level when the
stepdown ladder has none there. A level within 1e-6 mm of the tab top
becomes the tab top itself (0.2 mm steps gave -3.0000000000000004, a
level under the tab top that carried the tabs). The closed contour and
the whole-model contour read ring_levels. The open runs have no tabs
and keep levels.

Pins: crates/motion/tests/contour_tab_height.rs measures the tab height
from the posted moves for a stepdown larger and smaller than the tab
height. Four old pins and the first-router-part example follow the
added pass.

Fixes #2579

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
